<title>POLAND: Polish 1996 rapeseed production falls to 500,000 T.</title>
<headline>Polish 1996 rapeseed production falls to 500,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland produced 500,000 tonnes of rapeseed production in 1996, 900,000 tonnes less than in 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said in an output estimate report on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The fall in rapeseed production is a result of a drop in the area sown against last year,&quot; the GUS report said.</p>
<p>Farmers have sown 278,000 hectares with rapeseed this year against 606,000 hectares in 1995. The drop in rapeseed area followed a harsh winter which made farmers replough their rapeseed fields and sow sugar beets instead.</p>
<p>-- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
